Z||000000||1FST2M6||12-29-2000||08:31 AM||||ok sitting in traffic in front of the mall. there are 5 lanes of traffic leaving.. i'm in the very center lane. the lanes to the right are going to I-75 and the lanes to the left are going straight down the "strip". there are about 20 people in the starbucks/Rio Bravo parking lot that watched us leave (all honda/mustang friends). Lynds stopped with 2 cars in front of us at the light... to my left pulls up 3 kids in an Altima. ahead of them is a 95+ Exploder Eddie Bauer. the lanes to the right DON'T have a light so they are inching fwd to the interstate on-ramp.. she had probly 8-10ft from the car in front of us to our bumper... While these kids were staring at my car, hootin and hollerin, reving their pea shooter to oblivion, Lynds taps the gas to pull forward a bit, the kids hear the rpms increase in the Fiero while not looking fwd just out their passenger side window and dump the clutch in their car BOOOOM SMASH right in to the back of some innocent lady stoped not 5' in ftont of them!  Dumb @$$es!  Moral of the story... if you hear some gimp kids reving their engine behind you.. brace yourself...   the lady was ok but the Altima was towed away and the kids 'rents had to come pick them up... (15,17 and 17) <P><BR>(oh if you didn't notice Lynds was driving... I had a few margaritas at Rio Bravo)<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig1fst.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||GT Bastard||12-29-2000||08:39 AM||||Whew, for a second I thought the Cheeto has been IN the accident.  That's about the funniest thing I've heard in weeks! Especially the part about Lynds driving your dunk-a$$ home!  hehe...  Did it look like anyone was hurt?  Man, it's people like that who make me lose faith in mankind.||||reg||1
