Z||000028||BN Boomer||01-24-2001||12:19 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fiero56:<BR><B>Perhaps the yuppy soccer mom on the phone? I can go on. Doesn't matter what I'm driving, bigger than them or smaller, they get no respect from me. Ain't gonna' change my view either. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Just out of curiosity, what in the hell does any of that rant have to do with SUVs or 4WDs? Or are you suggesting that it's okay to behave like that in a mini-van or car but not in an SUV?<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B><BR>99% of SUV owners should be driving mini-vans. Minivans serve the purpose better in every aspect, for those 99%...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well, maybe 99% of Fiero owners should be driving Altimas.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> After all, they are more visible to other drivers, handle inclement weather better, probably get better fuel economy, and are just plain more versatile. So what was your argument again? Something about suitability? I guess that only applies to everyone else, huh? <P>||||reg||1
