Z||000030||jerpro||01-24-2001||04:03 PM||||It is not the SUV it is the driver.<BR>I was going down the highway last thursday, and a red suv with a blonde on the phone gets into the highway. She immediately tries to get on the fast lane. I am in the middle lane right in front of her and see through my rearview how she barely misses the white car on the fast lane, swerves right and starts spinning and lands on the roof. I was the last car in front of her and everyone behind me had to stop. They took 5hrs to clean up the mess.<BR>How many SUV's and 4WD do you see out in the ditches in the winter?<BR>It all has to do with the stupid "I own the road" drivers. Take them out of the road and then I will say that SUV's and 4WD are great cars for their purpose.<BR>Will you take a fiero off roading (I hope not...)<BR>Then, why do you put an suv on a highway at 80mph????<P>DId you guys hear about the AMG/mercedes-benz ML55 SUV? It is told to be able to go 150 mph!!!!!!!! You better be a great driver not to get in a n accident at 150 mph on a suv.... Imagine if you put a woman with 4 kids.......<P>I agree with the majority, SUv's and 4WD suck and they are better out of production, they are more hazardous than 90 year old grandmas in lincons.<P>By the way...... I could beat an altima in reverse   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR>------------------<BR>Only try your best, and if at first you don't succeed... TRY HARDER.<p>[This message has been edited by jerpro (edited 01-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000031||Seanh||01-25-2001||01:11 AM||||I would have to strongly disagree here, I love SUV's and 4wds. In the winter time my Ford Bronco has saved my life (and a$$) more then once. I wouldnt give up a 4x4 in the grauge for nothin. Its all in the driver. A Geo metro can kill people just as easily as an SUV can with a bad driver. This all goes back to: "Guns dont kill people, people kill people" It takes a bad driver behind the wheel to kill someone, not the vehical they are driving.||||reg||1
Z||000032||DaRkLoRD||01-25-2001||01:22 AM||||True, but a Suburban which drives into you at 80mph is gonna do a lot more damage than a Geo Metro going the same speed... and typically, people driving smaller cars aren't as likely to pull into a lane without checking if there's a car already there..<P>Once again, I do like SUVs... but most people don't actually need to drive the really huge ones.. some do, and they're usually the ones that are responsible with them.. it's the ones that aren't skilled in driving a large truck, and only have one because it's cool, that we're complaining about...<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||8
Z||000033||Seanh||01-25-2001||02:10 AM||||Well, I guess it is kinda a toss up. SUV's save lives by protecting people in an accident, and they also take lives when in the hands of the wrong drivers. Maybe some pecautions should be taken, like requiring an endoresment on your licence to drive larger trucks/suv's. Obtained by attending a driving school, geared tword safe handling a large truck.<P>I do agree, there is a certain state of mind while driveing a tank. I am a little more carefree in my Bronco then in the Fiero. Not because the bronco is bigger, just because the Fiero is alot smaller.<P>I dont know here, reading back trough this thread since I cant seem to fall asleep. I in no way think suv's should be removed from the market, or restrictions on how large they can really be. I mean, Darklord has a good point about it, but we dont drive Fieros because we have to, becaue we want to. In stock form they are pretty fast, and most have made improvments to get more power and speed. I think more driving education is the key, not restricting the type of vehical someone can buy.<p>[This message has been edited by Seanh (edited 01-25-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000034||ur2biteme||01-25-2001||02:21 AM||||well, all i know is that this topic got brought up out of nowhere.  i personally dont care if your second car(or primary car for a few people involved) is an altima, suburban, metro, whatever.  this topic is getting beat to death.  my only statement on the matter is actually a question:  If more steel and a higher stance equals a safer car, then why is it that volvo's seem to always be the safest rated cars in america?  ||||reg||1
